[{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Describe the following linear transformations:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>It is given that the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Write down the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^{2025}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^2=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^3=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A^{2025}=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>A shape with area 4 is mapped to its image by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Write down the area of the shape’s image.</p>","steps":["<p>The matrix represents a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis. So the image will have the same area as the original shape. So the area of the shape’s image is 4 units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Write down the matrix that represents a reflection that maps:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-6,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-9,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-4,-7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-7,-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,5)\\mapsto(3,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-6,-2)\\mapsto(6,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,9)\\mapsto(-9,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-4,-7)\\mapsto(-7,-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has vertices at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(10,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is reflected in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Using matrices, find the coordinates of the vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}8&amp;9&amp;10\\\\1&amp;3&amp;-3\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;3&amp;-3\\\\8&amp;9&amp;10\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So the coordinates of the vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>The trapezium <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has vertices at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(11,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is reflected in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis to form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Using matrices, find the coordinates of the vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;6&amp;11&amp;-1\\\\5&amp;5&amp;-3&amp;-3\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;6&amp;11&amp;-1\\\\-5&amp;-5&amp;3&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So the coordinates of the vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(11,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Use a matrix method to reflect the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the line with equation:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=8-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>First reflect the point in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\-5\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-5\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The vector from the origin to the closest point on the line is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-2.5\\\\2.5\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  So the position vector of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when reflected in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}-5\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}+2\\begin{pmatrix}-2.5\\\\2.5\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-10\\\\8\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(-10,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>First reflect the point in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\-5\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\-3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The vector from the origin to the closest point on the line is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  So the position vector of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when reflected in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=8-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\-3\\end{pmatrix}+2\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}13\\\\5\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(13,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Write down the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\times2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> matrix that represents:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>A reflection in the line that makes an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the horizontal.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line that makes an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"60^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the horizontal.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line that makes an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the horizontal.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line that makes an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"75^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the horizontal.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\times30^\\circ)&amp;\\sin(2\\times30^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(2\\times30^\\circ)&amp;-\\cos(2\\times30^\\circ)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos60^\\circ&amp;\\sin60^\\circ\\\\\\sin60^\\circ&amp;-\\cos60^\\circ\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac12&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;-\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\times60^\\circ)&amp;\\sin(2\\times60^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(2\\times60^\\circ)&amp;-\\cos(2\\times60^\\circ)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos120^\\circ&amp;\\sin120^\\circ\\\\\\sin120^\\circ&amp;-\\cos120^\\circ\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac12&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\times15^\\circ)&amp;\\sin(2\\times15^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(2\\times15^\\circ)&amp;-\\cos(2\\times15^\\circ)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos30^\\circ&amp;\\sin30^\\circ\\\\\\sin30^\\circ&amp;-\\cos30^\\circ\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;\\frac12\\\\\\frac12&amp;-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\times75^\\circ)&amp;\\sin(2\\times75^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(2\\times75^\\circ)&amp;-\\cos(2\\times75^\\circ)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos150^\\circ&amp;\\sin150^\\circ\\\\\\sin150^\\circ&amp;-\\cos150^\\circ\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;\\frac12\\\\\\frac12&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Write down the matrix that represents the following linear transformations:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac18x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac15x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>A reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac{x}{5\\sqrt3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=\\sqrt2\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\arctan\\sqrt2=54.7^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\arctan\\sqrt2)&amp;\\sin(2\\arctan\\sqrt2)\\\\\\sin(2\\arctan\\sqrt2)&amp;-\\cos(2\\arctan\\sqrt2)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac13&amp;\\frac{2\\sqrt2}3\\\\\\frac{2\\sqrt2}3&amp;\\frac13\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-0.333&amp;0.943\\\\0.943&amp;0.333\\end{pmatrix}\\quad(3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=3\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\arctan3=71.6^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\arctan3)&amp;\\sin(2\\arctan3)\\\\\\sin(2\\arctan3)&amp;-\\cos(2\\arctan3)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac45&amp;\\frac35\\\\\\frac35&amp;\\frac45\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-0.8&amp;0.6\\\\0.6&amp;0.8\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=\\frac18\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\arctan\\frac18=7.13^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\arctan\\frac18)&amp;\\sin(2\\arctan\\frac18)\\\\\\sin(2\\arctan\\frac18)&amp;-\\cos(2\\arctan\\frac18)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{63}{65}&amp;\\frac{16}{65}\\\\\\frac{16}{65}&amp;-\\frac{63}{65}\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0.969&amp;0.246\\\\0.246&amp;-0.969\\end{pmatrix}\\quad(3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\arctan\\frac1{\\sqrt3}=30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos60^\\circ&amp;\\sin60^\\circ\\\\\\sin60^\\circ&amp;-\\cos60^\\circ\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac12&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;-\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0.500&amp;0.866\\\\0.866&amp;-0.500\\end{pmatrix}\\quad(3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=-2\\Rightarrow\\theta=180^\\circ+\\arctan(-2)=117^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-2)))&amp;\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-2)))\\\\\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-2)))&amp;-\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-2)))\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac35&amp;-\\frac45\\\\-\\frac45&amp;\\frac35\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=\\begin{pmatrix}-0.6&amp;-0.8\\\\-0.8&amp;0.6\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{\\sqrt2})=145^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{\\sqrt2})))&amp;\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{\\sqrt2})))\\\\\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{\\sqrt2})))&amp;-\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{\\sqrt2})))\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac13&amp;-\\frac{2\\sqrt2}3\\\\-\\frac{2\\sqrt2}3&amp;-\\frac13\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0.333&amp;-0.943\\\\-0.943&amp;-0.333\\end{pmatrix}\\quad(3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=-\\frac15\\Rightarrow\\theta=180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac15)=169^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac15)))&amp;\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac15)))\\\\\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac15)))&amp;-\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac15)))\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{12}{13}&amp;-\\frac5{13}\\\\-\\frac5{13}&amp;-\\frac{12}{13}\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0.923&amp;-0.385\\\\-0.385&amp;-0.923\\end{pmatrix}\\quad(3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">h)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=-\\frac1{5\\sqrt3}\\Rightarrow\\theta=180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{5\\sqrt3})=173^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{5\\sqrt3})))&amp;\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{5\\sqrt3})))\\\\\\sin(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{5\\sqrt3})))&amp;-\\cos(2(180^\\circ+\\arctan(-\\frac1{5\\sqrt3})))\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{37}{38}&amp;-\\frac{5\\sqrt3}{38}\\\\-\\frac{5\\sqrt3}{38}&amp;-\\frac{37}{38}\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0.974&amp;-0.228\\\\-0.228&amp;-0.974\\end{pmatrix}\\quad(3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the mirror line for each of these matrices in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=kx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given to 3 significant figures:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;\\frac12\\\\\\frac12&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;-\\frac12\\\\-\\frac12&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}4&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}4\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}4&amp;-\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}4&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}4\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}4&amp;-\\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos2\\theta=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{75^\\circ,105^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin2\\theta=\\frac12\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{15^\\circ,75^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=75^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  So the mirror line has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(\\tan75^\\circ)x\\Rightarrow y=(2+\\sqrt3)x\\Rightarrow y=3.73x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos2\\theta=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{75^\\circ,105^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin2\\theta=-\\frac12\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{105^\\circ,165^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=105^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  So the mirror line has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(\\tan105^\\circ)x\\Rightarrow y=(-2-\\sqrt3)x\\Rightarrow y=-3.73x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos2\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}4\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{7.5^\\circ,172.5^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin2\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}4\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{7.5^\\circ,82.5^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=7.5^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  So the mirror line has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(\\tan7.5^\\circ)x\\Rightarrow y=0.132x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos2\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}4\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{37.5^\\circ,142.5^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin2\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}4\\Rightarrow\\theta=\\{37.5^\\circ,52.5^\\circ\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=37.5^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  So the mirror line has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(\\tan37.5^\\circ)x\\Rightarrow y=0.767x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is mapped to the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3+2\\sqrt3,2-3\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=kx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix that represents this transformation.</p>","steps":["<p>Midpoint of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3+2\\sqrt3,2-3\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac72+\\sqrt3,4-\\frac32\\sqrt3\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  Gradient from the origin to the midpoint is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{4-\\frac32\\sqrt3}{\\frac72+\\sqrt3}=2-\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The angle the mirror line makes with the horizontal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\arctan(2-\\sqrt3)=15^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\times15^\\circ)&amp;\\sin(2\\times15^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(2\\times15^\\circ)&amp;-\\cos(2\\times15^\\circ)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos30^\\circ&amp;\\sin30^\\circ\\\\\\sin30^\\circ&amp;-\\cos30^\\circ\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;\\frac12\\\\\\frac12&amp;-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-18,20)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is mapped to the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9+10\\sqrt3,10-9\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=kx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix that represents this transformation.</p>","steps":["<p>Midpoint of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-18,20)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9+10\\sqrt3,10-9\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(-\\frac92+5\\sqrt3,15-\\frac92\\sqrt3\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  Gradient from the origin to the midpoint is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{15-\\frac92\\sqrt3}{-\\frac92+5\\sqrt3}=\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The angle the mirror line makes with the horizontal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\arctan\\sqrt3=60^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\times60^\\circ)&amp;\\sin(2\\times60^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(2\\times60^\\circ)&amp;-\\cos(2\\times60^\\circ)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos120^\\circ&amp;\\sin120^\\circ\\\\\\sin120^\\circ&amp;-\\cos120^\\circ\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac12&amp;\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&amp;\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\times2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, writing each element in an exact form not involving trigonometry.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=\\frac41\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\sin\\theta=\\frac4{\\sqrt{17}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=\\frac1{\\sqrt{17}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos2\\theta=2\\cos^2\\theta-1=2\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt{17}}\\right)^2-1=-\\frac{15}{17}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=2\\times\\frac4{\\sqrt{17}}\\times\\frac1{\\sqrt{17}}=\\frac8{17}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac{15}{17}&amp;\\frac8{17}\\\\\\frac8{17}&amp;\\frac{15}{17}\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.38-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=kx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{1-k^2}{1+k^2}&amp;\\frac{2k}{1+k^2}\\\\\\frac{2k}{1+k^2}&amp;\\frac{k^2-1}{1+k^2}\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\sin\\theta=\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=\\frac1{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\cos2\\theta=\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta=\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\\right)^2=\\frac1{1+k^2}-\\frac{k^2}{1+k^2}=\\frac{1-k^2}{1+k^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=2\\left(\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\\right)\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\\right)=\\frac{2k}{1+k^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos2\\theta&amp;\\sin2\\theta\\\\\\sin2\\theta&amp;-\\cos2\\theta\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{1-k^2}{1+k^2}&amp;\\frac{2k}{1+k^2}\\\\\\frac{2k}{1+k^2}&amp;-\\frac{1-k^2}{1+k^2}\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{1-k^2}{1+k^2}&amp;\\frac{2k}{1+k^2}\\\\\\frac{2k}{1+k^2}&amp;\\frac{k^2-1}{1+k^2}\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]}]